So, after a couple of weeks of trying to play a Wizard, and failing
miserably, I said, screw it, I'll play another combat-wombat type,
just to prove I'm not a complete idiot, and that it's just the
difference between spellcasters and destructive machines that is my
problem.

And, it turns out, that's probably exactly right.  This is my third
ascension, a Barbarian after a Valk and a Samurai.  Hrm.

The early game was quite uneventful.  Stole a ]oMR and ]GoP very early
on, which didn't hurt at all.  Found a BoH lying around somewhere...
and of course there was another in Sokoban.  Never did find a
"oReflection the whole game.

Did Sokoban first, then the mines.  Cross-aligned altar in Minetown,
of course.  Had a bit of fun at Mine's End, as some of the locations
with gems had already been dug out by dwarves.  Damned dwarves.  I did
get, and eventually identify, the luckstone, though it would soon
enough not matter.

Cross-aligned altar on 6, co-aligned on 7, crossed *temple* on 10. 
This priestess of Mitra sold me 12 points of protection, and what did
she get for it?  Killed, her altar converted, and I would've stolen
the 80k or so gold back if it weren't so darn heavy.

Found the portal to Ludios after some searching, and cleaned it out. 
That's where I picked up the orange dragon scales which later became
ODSM.  By the time I got to this point, I had reflection from a
shield, thanks to an Aleax, and MR from the cloak, so I figured, why
waste a wish on GDSM or SDSM when I can use an enchant armor scroll on
these orange scales and get points for style?  (Or lack thereof.)

Got down to Medusa's level before killing enough things--and eating a
couple of wraiths--to get me to XL 14.  Sacrificed for Cleaver and
Fire Brand... well, better than nothing.  Of course, in the meantime I
summoned both Yeenoghu AND Juiblex, without meaning to.  But hey,
peaceful demon lords are a good thing.

Went on the quest, the only major problem with which was those damned
trolls.  Isn't there any good way to stop them regenerating?  Thoth
Amon, though, was a pushover.

Went back up for a while, sacrificed for Frost Brand--much better. 
Headed down, destroyed Medusa, and broke into the Castle from the
rear, using the Heart's nifty levitation ability.  The castle wand was
0:1... yuk.  2 scrolls of charging, a magic marker, blessed ring of
levitation, speed boots (after, of course, losing mine to accidentally
not taking them off before readin an enchant armor), and a crystal
ball.  I just remember I had to hold down the 'z' key for quite a
while to wrest out that final wish (for the crystal ball).  I must've
quaffed a dozen blessed smoky potions looking for other wishes, and
never got one. :(

Asmodeus got statued; Baalzebub level-teleported out.  I later found
him on DLvl 3--during my ascension run.  Ugh.  Juiblex's swamp was
empty, of course.  Orcus wasn't too much challenge.  I had a devil of
a time finding Vlad's staircase, eventually finding it hidden behind a
boulder--and then had the same trouble finding the downstair a couple
levels later.  This made for the least fun part of the game.  I hate
Gehennom.

After all that, though, it was pretty smooth sailing until the
Sanctum.  A number of foo-liches assaulted my a number of times, and
now I see why people genocide them so often... but, then, I had
decided to go genoless, and all my scrolls of genocide got cursed and
used to summon nurses (which netted me about 200 HP).  Killed Rodney
outside his tower, grabbed the book, opened the sanctum... and headed
down.

Getting in was no problem, though a foo-lich dogged me on the way in. 
Getting out was a different matter.  I was ganged up on by:  the high
priest of Moloch, two Rodneys, and two arch-liches.  Used about six
B!oFH getting out of there, one very slow step at a time.  Thankfully,
I was able to find the Amulet in that Charlie-Foxtrot.  I think the
liches alone had me surrounded my various nasties; two Rodneys was
just, well, whatever the opposite of icing is.

Then, I ran like hell.  Rodney only showed up a few more times, though
one arch-lich was determined to follow me up the stairs as far as he
could.  The mysterious force kicked in on 47... and 47... and 47...
and 47!... and then again on 46!... and only once after that.  But
DLvl 47 was quickly becoming my least favorite hangout.

Astral... my guardian angel was waiting for me.  On with the
blindfold... Famine to the right, Pestilence to the middle, Death on
the left.  I was on the left-middle... and stuff started streaming
right out of the middle.  I figured the choice had been made for me. 
After hanging around the entrance picking them off one at a time, I
stormed through the few remaining priests, up to the high altar... and
it was the right one.

I made it to the demigods' bar with three more beers, wearing spiffy
bright orange armor.  That's right, orange.  You wanna argue fashion
with someone named Conan?

